<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Supplementary Material</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1. </span>Derivation for NSR updates on entirely-incorrect groups</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="In Gradient characterization. ‣ 3.2. Negative Sample Reinforcement (NSR) for Entirely-Incorrect Groups ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) from the EGPO objective (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.1.3. Base advantage, calibrated advantage, and objective ‣ 3.1. Entropy-Guided Policy Optimization (EGPO) ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>)) on an entirely-incorrect group.
We consider one group <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{-}(x)=\{(x,y_{i},r_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{-}(x)=\{(x,y_{i},r_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under NSR, the base advantage is <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.2. Negative Sample Reinforcement (NSR) for Entirely-Incorrect Groups ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>)), and the calibrated advantage becomes</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{A}_{i}\;=\;w_{i}A_{i}\;=\;-w_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{A}_{i}\;=\;w_{i}A_{i}\;=\;-w_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Clipped objective term.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For one sampled response <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the per-response term in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.1.3. Base advantage, calibrated advantage, and objective ‣ 3.1. Entropy-Guided Policy Optimization (EGPO) ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) is</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(\theta)=\min\Big(\rho_{i}(\theta)\,\tilde{A}_{i},\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\,\tilde{A}_{i}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(\theta)=\min\Big(\rho_{i}(\theta)\,\tilde{A}_{i},\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\,\tilde{A}_{i}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{A}_{i}=-w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{A}_{i}=-w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell_{i}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell_{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\Big(\rho_{i}(\theta)\,(-w_{i}),\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\,(-w_{i})\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="1.600em">,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\Big(\rho_{i}(\theta)\,(-w_{i}),\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\,(-w_{i})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-w_{i}\,\max\Big(\rho_{i}(\theta),\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-w_{i}\,\max\Big(\rho_{i}(\theta),\;\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the equality follows because multiplying by a negative scalar reverses the order.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Effect of clipping.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\rho_{i}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\rho_{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definition of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{clip}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{clip}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{clip}(\rho,1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)=\begin{cases}1-\epsilon,&amp;\rho&lt;1-\epsilon,\\
\rho,&amp;1-\epsilon\leq\rho\leq 1+\epsilon,\\
1+\epsilon,&amp;\rho&gt;1+\epsilon.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{clip}(\rho,1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)=\begin{cases}1-\epsilon,&amp;\rho&lt;1-\epsilon,\\
\rho,&amp;1-\epsilon\leq\rho\leq 1+\epsilon,\\
1+\epsilon,&amp;\rho&gt;1+\epsilon.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Plugging Eq. (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Effect of clipping. ‣ A.1. Derivation for NSR updates on entirely-incorrect groups ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) into Eq. (<a href="#A1.E18" title="In Clipped objective term. ‣ A.1. Derivation for NSR updates on entirely-incorrect groups ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) gives three cases:
(i) if <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&lt;1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&lt;1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(\rho,\mathrm{clip}(\rho))=1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(\rho,\mathrm{clip}(\rho))=1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(\theta)=-w_{i}(1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(\theta)=-w_{i}(1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> is constant in <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, thus contributing zero gradient;
(ii) if <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\epsilon\leq\rho\leq 1+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\epsilon\leq\rho\leq 1+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{clip}(\rho)=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{clip}(\rho)=\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(\theta)=-w_{i}\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(\theta)=-w_{i}\rho</annotation></semantics></math>;
(iii) if <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;1+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;1+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{clip}(\rho)=1+\epsilon&lt;\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{clip}(\rho)=1+\epsilon&lt;\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(\theta)=-w_{i}\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(\theta)=-w_{i}\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, for negative advantages on entirely-incorrect groups, clipping is active only when <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&lt;1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&lt;1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise the objective reduces to</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(\theta)\;=\;-w_{i}\,\rho_{i}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(\theta)\;=\;-w_{i}\,\rho_{i}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gradient direction in the unclipped region.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the gradient of Eq. (<a href="#A1.E20" title="In Effect of clipping. ‣ A.1. Derivation for NSR updates on entirely-incorrect groups ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).
Since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}(\theta)=\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}\mid x)/\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}(\theta)=\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}\mid x)/\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> is constant w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\rho_{i}(\theta)}{\partial z_{v}}=\rho_{i}(\theta)\,\frac{\partial\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}\mid x)}{\partial z_{v}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\rho_{i}(\theta)}{\partial z_{v}}=\rho_{i}(\theta)\,\frac{\partial\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}\mid x)}{\partial z_{v}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover,</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}\mid x)=\sum_{t=1}^{T_{i}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}\mid x)=\sum_{t=1}^{T_{i}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">At a fixed step <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> be the softmax probability of token <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x,y_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x,y_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> the corresponding logit.
The standard softmax derivative gives</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t})}{\partial z_{v}}=\mathbf{1}[v=y_{t}]-\pi_{v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t})}{\partial z_{v}}=\mathbf{1}[v=y_{t}]-\pi_{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A1.E20" title="In Effect of clipping. ‣ A.1. Derivation for NSR updates on entirely-incorrect groups ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>)–Eq. (<a href="#A1.E23" title="In Gradient direction in the unclipped region. ‣ A.1. Derivation for NSR updates on entirely-incorrect groups ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial\ell_{i}(\theta)}{\partial z_{v}}=-w_{i}\,\frac{\partial\rho_{i}(\theta)}{\partial z_{v}}=-w_{i}\,\rho_{i}(\theta)\big(\mathbf{1}[v=y_{t}]-\pi_{v}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\ell_{i}(\theta)}{\partial z_{v}}=-w_{i}\,\frac{\partial\rho_{i}(\theta)}{\partial z_{v}}=-w_{i}\,\rho_{i}(\theta)\big(\mathbf{1}[v=y_{t}]-\pi_{v}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Since EGPO maximizes Eq. (<a href="#S3.E12" title="In 3.1.3. Base advantage, calibrated advantage, and objective ‣ 3.1. Entropy-Guided Policy Optimization (EGPO) ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), the gradient ascent direction on logits is</p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{EGPO}}{\partial z_{v}}\propto w_{i}\,\rho_{i}(\theta)\big(\mathbf{1}[v=y_{t}]-\pi_{v}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∝</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{EGPO}}{\partial z_{v}}\propto w_{i}\,\rho_{i}(\theta)\big(\mathbf{1}[v=y_{t}]-\pi_{v}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which matches Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="In Gradient characterization. ‣ 3.2. Negative Sample Reinforcement (NSR) for Entirely-Incorrect Groups ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Know What You Know: Metacognitive Entropy Calibration for Verifiable RL Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
In particular, the sampled token <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is pushed down while probability mass is redistributed to other tokens, yielding a consistent negative update direction on entirely-incorrect groups.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2. </span>Dataset Construction: OpenR1-Math Stable-10k</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We load OpenR1-Math shards <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hugging Face, 2025</a>)</cite> consisting of default and extended subsets, construct candidates with heavy filtering, apply (optional) test-set decontamination and internal deduplication via MinHash-LSH, then sample a 10k pool with subset/bucket/source constraints, and finally split out a small validation set. The goal is to produce an RL compatible pool with reduced reward noise and controlled coverage. This process yields the training dataset OpenR1-Stable-10k.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We observed that for Qwen2.5-Math (4096 context length), over 99% of generated responses stay below 2500 tokens. Therefore, even with the longest prompts, the total context length remains well, and no special length adjustment beyond the standard prompt filtering is required.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 4</span>. </span><span id="A1.T4.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Construction recipe for the <span id="A1.T4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OpenR1-Stable-10k</span> training dataset.</span></figcaption>
